hadiths[6]{hadithnumber,text}:
"22235","Waki narrated to us, Hisham ibn Sad narrated to us, Yazid ibn Nuaym ibn Hazzal informed me, from his father, he said: Maiz ibn Malik was in the custody of my father, and he fell upon a slave girl of the tribe. My father said to him: Go to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and inform him of what you did, perhaps he will seek forgiveness for you, intending thereby hope that there would be a way out for him. He came to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, I have committed adultery, so carry out the Book of Allah upon me. He turned away from him. Then he came to him a second time and said: O Messenger of Allah, I have committed adultery, so carry out the Book of Allah upon me. Then he came to him a third time and said: O Messenger of Allah, I have committed adultery, so carry out the Book of Allah upon me. Then he came to him a fourth time and said: O Messenger of Allah, I have committed adultery, so carry out the Book of Allah upon me. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: You have said it four times, so with whom? He said: With so-and-so. He said: Did you lie with her? He said: Yes. He said: Did you touch her? He said: Yes. He said: Did you have intercourse with her? He said: Yes. He said: So he ordered him to be stoned. He said: So he was taken out to al-Harra, and when he was stoned and felt the touch of the stones, he panicked and ran off rushing. Abd Allah ibn Unays met him, and he had outdone his companions, so he pulled out for him the shank of a camel and threw it at him and killed him. He said: Then he came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and mentioned that to him, and he said: Would that you had left him, perhaps he would repent and Allah would turn to him. Hisham said: Yazid ibn Nuaym ibn Hazzal narrated to me, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to my father when he saw him: By Allah, O Hazzal, had you covered him with your garment, it would have been better than what you did with him."
"22236","Affan narrated to us, Aban, meaning Ibn Yazid al-Attar, narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to me, from Abu Salama ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Nuaym ibn Hazzal, that Hazzal had hired Maiz ibn Malik, and he had a slave girl called Fatima who had been married, and she used to herd sheep for them, and Maiz fell upon her. He informed Hazzal, so he deceived him and said: Go to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and inform him, perhaps a Quran will descend about you. The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, ordered him and he was stoned. When the touch of the stones hurt him, he set off running, and a man met him with the jawbone of a camel or the leg of a camel and struck him with it and knocked him down. The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Woe to you, O Hazzal, had you covered him with your garment, it would have been better for you."
"22237","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Yazid ibn Nuaym, from his father, that Maiz ibn Malik came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: Carry out the Book of Allah upon me. He turned away from him four times, then ordered his stoning. When the stones touched him, Abd al-Rahman said, and he said once: When the stones hurt him, he panicked and ran off rushing, and Abd Allah ibn Unays, or Anas ibn Nadiya, came out and threw him with the shank of a donkey and knocked him down. He came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and informed him of his matter, and he said: Would that you had left him, perhaps he would repent and Allah would turn to him. Then he said: O Hazzal, had you covered him with your garment, it would have been better for you."
"22238","Waki narrated to us, Hisham ibn Said narrated to us, Yazid ibn Nuaym ibn Hazzal informed me, from his father, that Maiz ibn Malik was in his custody. He said: When he committed adultery, he said to him: Go to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and inform him. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to him when he met him: O Hazzal, had you covered him with your garment, it would have been better than what you did with him."
"22239","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us, Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, he said: I heard Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir narrating from Ibn Hazzal, from his father, that he mentioned something of the matter of Maiz to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Had you covered him with your garment, it would have been better for you."
"22240","Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Tayalisi narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Said, he said: I heard Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir narrating from Ibn Hazzal, from his father, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said to him: Woe to you, O Hazzal, had you covered him, meaning Maiz, with your garment, it would have been better for you."
